# Deterministic boot: title screen -> tutorial, three frame dumps, clean quit.
#
# The host applies events when the presented-frame counter reaches the number in
# column one.  `waitsteady` pauses the script until the draw count has not
# changed for N frames (optionally with a minimum draw count), and later frame
# numbers are counted from that sync point.  That keeps the script independent
# of startup timing and GPU shader-compile hitches.
#
# Title screen: ~150 draws.  Tutorial: ~500+ draws.  The default startup
# build is slow because the tutorial's hot path falls back to Unicorn, so keep
# the post-sync window short; use --full when fps matters.
0 waitsteady 20 100
60 tap 57
120 waitsteady 30 400
360 dump
480 dump
600 dump
660 quit
